  "body": "Replication got a bit slow, and then there were lots of these in the logs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/matrix/synapse/synapse/replication/tcp/protocol.py\", line 468, in subscribe_to_stream\r\n    if token > current_token:\r\nTypeError: '>' not supported between instances of 'NoneType' and 'int'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is coming from https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a163b748a5ca37853f440c5c46d2da80f738a9e0/synapse/replication/tcp/protocol.py#L468. The problem is that this loop assumes that there are no pending updates with a null `token`; however in practice the pending list may contain batches of updates as per https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a163b748a5ca37853f440c5c46d2da80f738a9e0/synapse/replication/tcp/resource.py#L289.\r\n\r\nWe probably need to unpack the batches to decide whether to send them.",
